from "../phonebook.rq" import phonebook

support_page {
    Rank actions by ease and likelihood to nudge. Star on GitHub is first.
    Default view is a graph. Toggle Graph / Tiles / Table as icon buttons on the right of the header, with hover tooltips.
    Graph: cola layout, settled on first paint to the visible window; copy has no graph coordinates; each node moves with its label; nodes are draggable; a drop keeps the new position; a drag does not start the action; all nodes offset slightly toward the cursor; nodes repel so some canvas edges stay open; action radius is impact × ease and stays latent to users; action nodes are solid and flat; each action links to a smaller passive original-group node in secondary colour (advocacy, community, cite, contribute, sponsor); group labels grow on group hover; labels do not overlap.
    Hover on an action node shows a tooltip with the action blurb.
    Star and sponsor tags are featured in the orange brand colour: the Star action, sponsor actions, and the Sponsor group.
    Tiles: responsive flex layout.
    Table: action and group only. Ease, impact, and score stay latent.
    Action names use the aqua link colour in Graph, Tiles, and Table, including copy and share, except featured graph tags.
    Each table row runs the same action as the graph and tiles: open a link, copy, or share.
    Support via, in tile order:
    - one click
        - star on github
        - share
        - discord
    - a minute
        - cite
        - issues
        - post your certificate
        - say something nice on the Visual Studio Marketplace
        - say something nice on Open VSX
        - FREE stickers: show the world you are a reqling, via [phonebook] sticker-form
    - write
        - reach out and send an email
        - write a testimonial
    - sponsor
        - github sponsorship
        - direct sponsorship
    integrated with [phonebook].
    Copy lives in ["../../site/src/content/support.ts"] per ["./site.rq".copy].
    The site exposes `/support/` as a statically generated page.
    Sidebar nests Support section anchors as same-page children per ["./site.rq".sidebar_nav].
    Landing nav graph includes Support as a page node per ["./site.rq".nav_graph].
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["@/site/src/app/support/page.tsx"]
        ["@/site/src/views/SupportPage.tsx"]
        ["@/site/src/views/SupportGraph.tsx"]
        ["@/site/src/views/SupportTable.tsx"]
        ["@/site/src/views/support.module.css"]
        ["@/site/src/content/support.ts"]
        ["@/site/src/lib/support-action.ts"]
        ["@/site/src/lib/support-graph-cola.ts"]
        ["@/site/src/content/nav.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["@/site/src/content/support.test.ts"]
        ["@/site/src/lib/support-graph-cola.test.ts"]
    )
}
